  "summary": "Public records obtained from a Ball State University Flock network audit show Florida Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission police, deputized under 287(g), performed dozens of immigration-related Flock searches across thousands of agencies' camera networks. Several other state and county agencies (Texas DPS, Grant County IN, Lake County IN, Sarasota County FL, Brevard County FL, Nebraska State Patrol, Tennessee Highway Patrol, Fort Pierce FL, Mississippi DPS) also performed immigration-related searches, illustrating ICE's continued side-door access to Flock data despite Flock's claimed safeguards.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the Florida Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission police performed 38 different Flock searches for reasons that were listed as \"immigration.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "This highlights when you do mass surveillance, you really can't control the data",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "the sharp expansion of 287(g) has made that almost moot because a lot of local authorities are working so closely with ICE.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock has made changes to its network audits that makes each individual entry more vague, and authorities have warned police to be \"as vague as permissible\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    }
  ],
